{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/56144-if-onyx-path-had-a-volunteer-promotional-group-would-you-participate","id":56144,"title":"If Onyx Path had a volunteer promotional group, would you participate?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-23T08:19:24-08:00","id":56144,"title":"If Onyx Path had a volunteer promotional group, would you participate?","content":"Just last night, I was at my LGS hanging out, and met a person who introduced himself as a fan of Exalted. I was shocked to find that he was completely unaware of the new edition, the launch of Onyx Path, or indeed any information about the changes to the properties and products formerly produced by White Wolf. <br /> <br /> We were both in the store to play a tabletop miniatures game from a certain company who recruits volunteers from their player base to promote these games. These volunteers are vetted, and must prove a certain amount of commitment to the game, as well as signing NDAs to protect any intellectual property to which they may be exposed. In return, they are allowed to participate in playtests of new material, volunteer to man booths and run games at conventions, and get a discount on products for the company. <br /> <br /> This morning, I came across a thread in the Exalted forum, talking about the state of the RPG market, and the need for us, the fans, to better promote the games we love to help expand the market<br /> <br /> The two ideas fused in my brain, and now I am wondering if Onyx Path would benefit from setting up a similar volunteer corp. It could even be run by the volunteers, with oversight from Rich Thomas. I am wondering how many people would be interested in such a program, and would participate if one existed.<br /> <br /> Personally, I wouldn't bring up the idea if I wasn't interested, so coune me in! I would even volunteer to help administer the program.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> This one is for all my Exigents...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/102-lordwyrmsbane","name":"LordWyrmsBane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T08:40:26-08:00","id":56160,"title":"","content":"We're certainly looking into options, including working with the Wrecking Crew and other orgs to run demos at conventions (some cool stuff is on deck for Gen Con already, with details posted once things get finalized).<br /> <br /> Also, retailers can go to the Onyx Path website and check the FAQ for information on ordering PoD titles directly (i.e. not via traditional distribution). Plus every Onyx Path Kickstarter has Retailer tiers available.<br /> <br /> -MMM","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Owner/Editor - FlamesRising.com","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/949-matt-m-mcelroy","name":"Matt-M-McElroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar949_2.jpeg","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T09:16:39-08:00","id":56175,"title":"","content":"The last time I inquired about such a thing, which granted was back after Ex3 was first announced I got nothing official on the topic, unofficially directed to the Wrecking Crew who are the <a href=\"http://www.labynight2013.com/groups/the-wrecking-crew/\" target=\"_blank\">volunteer </a><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/pages/The-Wrecking-Crew/173603524675?ref=ts\" target=\"_blank\">demo </a>group. <br /> <br /> However apart from a couple of very brief dips into Scion (iirc, it's been a couple years, it might have been another non-exalted WW game) they only do WoD stuff and are very limited in what/where they cover.<br /> <br /> Determined to drum up interest I took the effort to hack down some of Exalted 2e into something convention playable, at least with the pre-gen characters I had. I asked around official peoples if there was any way I could offer a minor token or hand stuff out at the convention to help with the promotion of the game line. Nothing. Since everything is going through drive-thru I asked over there about the same, since I would basically be promoting the service. Some very minor item (bookmarks IIRC) was offered, never delivered.<br /> <br /> I spent a large part of that convention (outside of running the two games) updating people that no, White Wolf didn't close down back when the oWoD/cWoD ended. No they didn't get shut down. Yes they've actually been making stuff. And highlighting the quality of the books that were produced as Print On Demand. A lot of people were expecting some cheap coil-bound thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now personal experience aside, the problem with running a volunteer based administration is that by definition volunteers are flakier than a pie crust. When a choice has to be made between the volunteer work and something else, OPP is the loser. This gets into an issue given how much drudge work is involved in such an effort.<br /> <br /> <br /> So would OPP benefit? Probably. Would I be interested in such a program? Maybe if it had actual support sure. Do I think it's ever likely to get support? Well, between my own experiences and the fact that Exalted got less official advertising or promotion for it's kickstarter than any other product I've seen come out of White Wolf... I'm inclined to believe it's seen as some generally unpopular appendix to the world of darkness with an unusually fanatical fanbase, and thus attempting to increase or broaden the fanbase would be seen as a waste.<br /> <br /> <br /> So... if anything happens, I'd suspect it'll be all-fan driven. Some fans generating interesting scenarios and some characters to make it faster and easier to run something at a convention would be cool. Some people making a video Exalted Quick-start would be awesome. Someone getting Wil Wheaton to play it on one of his shows would be awesome. I'm thinking that anything more than those short-duration efforts are not likely to materialize. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T09:25:22-08:00","id":56183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/56144-if-onyx-path-had-a-volunteer-promotional-group-would-you-participate?p=56175#post56175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last time I inquired about such a thing, which granted was back after Ex3 was first announced I got nothing official on the topic, unofficially directed to the Wrecking Crew who are the <a href=\"http://www.labynight2013.com/groups/the-wrecking-crew/\" target=\"_blank\">volunteer </a><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/pages/The-Wrecking-Crew/173603524675?ref=ts\" target=\"_blank\">demo </a>group.<br /> <br /> However apart from a couple of very brief dips into Scion (iirc, it's been a couple years, it might have been another non-exalted WW game) they only do WoD stuff and are very limited in what/where they cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wrecking Crew has run demos of Exalted, Cavaliers of Mars and other non-World of Darkness games. It often depends on which volunteer Storytellers are attending the event in question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/56144-if-onyx-path-had-a-volunteer-promotional-group-would-you-participate?p=56175#post56175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now personal experience aside, the problem with running a volunteer based administration is that by definition volunteers are flakier than a pie crust. When a choice has to be made between the volunteer work and something else, OPP is the loser. This gets into an issue given how much drudge work is involved in such an effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, a good program would need lots of volunteers and OPP would need someone to coordinate with a large crew, vet the people and the process, follow-up with the team and conventions, deal with questions...all of which takes time and money (shipping isn't free, nor is printing).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/56144-if-onyx-path-had-a-volunteer-promotional-group-would-you-participate?p=56175#post56175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So would OPP benefit? Probably. Would I be interested in such a program? Maybe if it had actual support sure. Do I think it's ever likely to get support? Well, between my own experiences and the fact that <b>Exalted got less official advertising or promotion for it's kickstarter than any other product I've seen come out of White Wolf</b>... I'm inclined to believe it's seen as some generally unpopular appendix to the world of darkness with an unusually fanatical fanbase, and thus attempting to increase or broaden the fanbase would be seen as a waste.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did you get that idea? The E3 Kickstarter got more advertising than several of the WoD KS projects.<br /> <br /> -MMM","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Owner/Editor - FlamesRising.com","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/949-matt-m-mcelroy","name":"Matt-M-McElroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar949_2.jpeg","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T09:25:52-08:00","id":56185,"title":"","content":"I'm already on the volunteer promotional team. I pimp these games out to anyone willing to listen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T09:44:24-08:00","id":56196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt-M-McElroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/56144-if-onyx-path-had-a-volunteer-promotional-group-would-you-participate?p=56183#post56183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where did you get that idea? The E3 Kickstarter got more advertising than several of the WoD KS projects.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only form of advertising I saw outside of the website were posts put up by fans on public forums, people talking about how much money it was making after it started, and the couple different broad &quot;discussions&quot; that started up about previewed content... and that's stretching advertising to a very broad definition. It didn't even rate an update on the rpgnews.com feed unlike the WoD products. So if there was advertising it managed to completely miss me and anyone I asked in real life and apparently wasn't worth mentioning to me when I was sitting around commenting during the kickstarter about the lack of advertising and trying to work out the legality of fans creating and funding advertising for the product on our own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T09:49:50-08:00","id":56200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/56144-if-onyx-path-had-a-volunteer-promotional-group-would-you-participate?p=56196#post56196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only form of advertising <b>I saw</b> outside of the website were posts put up by fans on public forums, people talking about how much money it was making after it started, and the couple different broad &quot;discussions&quot; that started up about previewed content... and that's stretching advertising to a very broad definition.</div> </div> </div> </div>That you saw...which is the actual point here. Onyx Path had paid network advertising for the Exalted Kickstarter. Paid adds showed up on RPGnet and several other networked RPG and Geek media sites. Unfortunately you did not personally encounter those adds, but they certainly hit the web and were paid for by Onyx Path.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/56144-if-onyx-path-had-a-volunteer-promotional-group-would-you-participate?p=56196#post56196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It didn't even rate an update on the rpgnews.com feed unlike the WoD products. So if there was advertising it managed to completely miss me and anyone I asked in real life and apparently wasn't worth mentioning to me when I was sitting around commenting during the kickstarter about the lack of advertising and trying to work out the legality of fans creating and funding advertising for the product on our own.</div> </div> </div> </div>RPGNews.com is a volunteer blog/feed that gets updated when and if the owners have time, it should not be taken with any indication of authority on gaming news. You'll note it hasn't been updated for a while.<br /> <br /> -MMM","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Owner/Editor - FlamesRising.com","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/949-matt-m-mcelroy","name":"Matt-M-McElroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar949_2.jpeg","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T10:38:22-08:00","id":56223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt-M-McElroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/56144-if-onyx-path-had-a-volunteer-promotional-group-would-you-participate?p=56200#post56200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That you saw...which is the actual point here. Onyx Path had paid network advertising for the Exalted Kickstarter. Paid adds showed up on RPGnet and several other networked RPG and Geek media sites. Unfortunately you did not personally encounter those adds, but they certainly hit the web and were paid for by Onyx Path.</div> </div> </div> </div> That I saw and that anyone I repeatedly ask saw.<br /> <br /> If there was advertising that's great and on this I'd be happy to be wrong. However I was repeatedly asking people and talking about it in the IRC channel at the time, nobody of the couple dozen geeky Exalted fans ever mentioned seeing any advertising. <br /> <br /> <b>Update</b>: I've now found one person that saw it at the Five Days Left stage, so clearly I am wrong and it just happened to have missed the people I was asking at the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt-M-McElroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/56144-if-onyx-path-had-a-volunteer-promotional-group-would-you-participate?p=56200#post56200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RPGNews.com is a volunteer blog/feed that gets updated when and if the owners have time, it should not be taken with any indication of authority on gaming news. You'll note it hasn't been updated for a while.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes 11 days.<br /> <br /> And frankly this is a niche-market hobby. The closest thing to an actual authority on gaming news that exists is the various gaming companies periodically making blog posts. Someone that gathers the various company postings and blogs a summary is about as close as we get to a centralized distribution. This is why your own FlamesRising site spent at least a week at one point being the only source for an updated White Wolf production schedule.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's a stretch that if you have a product in a market where the only news outlets are unofficial fan-operated-as-I-have-time ones that you reach out to the people running those news outlets to make sure they cover it when you have news. Again, my opinion YMMV and so forth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T13:38:21-08:00","id":56334,"title":"","content":"How does one &quot;make sure&quot; they cover it?<br /> <br /> I ask because for a year I had a number of prominent sites and news outlets on a mailing list, and I'd let them know anytime we were doing anything major.<br /> <br /> We had zero return on that investment.<br /> <br /> We can't force people to cover us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T13:56:15-08:00","id":56344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/56144-if-onyx-path-had-a-volunteer-promotional-group-would-you-participate?p=56185#post56185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm already on the volunteer promotional team. I pimp these games out to anyone willing to listen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Same here, the clerk at my usual RPG seller is planning to kill me because I speak of the Onyx Path's new books to all the people searching for &quot;some good game, you know... the good, old-style ones&quot;<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T14:16:59-08:00","id":56359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/56144-if-onyx-path-had-a-volunteer-promotional-group-would-you-participate?p=56334#post56334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does one &quot;make sure&quot; they cover it?<br /> <br /> I ask because for a year I had a number of prominent sites and news outlets on a mailing list, and I'd let them know anytime we were doing anything major.<br /> <br /> We had zero return on that investment.</div> </div> </div> </div>So none of the sites you contacted ever covered anything you did? That would indicate that this list didn't include any of the sites that have covered stuff for you in the past, which seems a really odd list to run off of, a list of contacts pre-disposed to not covering you and that is the only people you attempt to contact.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/56144-if-onyx-path-had-a-volunteer-promotional-group-would-you-participate?p=56334#post56334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We can't force people to cover us.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course not, but some individualized follow up wouldn't likely be amiss. Something along the lines of &quot;Hey X, I want to thank you for the good coverage you've given us before and to ask if you had seen NewProduct and ask if you were going to do a write up on it and if there were any questions I could answer for you about it. Give me a call at (555) 555-5555&quot;. You're either apt to get &quot;Sorry, we're really busy over here&quot; or &quot;Oh hey I must have missed the press release about that one, have to look into what happened, yea send some info and I'll see what I can do&quot; or some other variant of rejection or polite form of &quot;whoops we were too busy to see that, let's fix that&quot;<br /> <br /> Now you guys may already be doing that and if so there's nothing really to add on that side of it. <br /> <br /> The lack of announcements/support from other RPG related news sites that normally cover everything OPP does might just be an anomaly. Since there's only been one book in the line kickstartered so far it's entirely possible it's just an inauspicious start rather than any sort of deliberate snubbing of the line. We'll find out whenever the next kickstarter in the line happens (hopefully this year).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T16:16:59-08:00","id":56409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt-M-McElroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/56144-if-onyx-path-had-a-volunteer-promotional-group-would-you-participate?p=56183#post56183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wrecking Crew has run demos of Exalted, Cavaliers of Mars and other non-World of Darkness games. It often depends on which volunteer Storytellers are attending the event in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you expand on some examples on the Exalted side? I had half an hour to kill while waiting for software to install, and I can only find two references via google, one to a guy called Jim who apparently joined the wrecking crew and got called &quot;The Exalted Guy&quot; and one game they ran at a convention back in 2009. going through the facebook page I can also find a lot of references to various WoD games they've run or plan to run, but nothing that mentions Cavaliers of Mars or anything non-WoD (apart from the one 2009 exalted game).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T17:12:59-08:00","id":56447,"title":"","content":"The Wrecking Crew might not be the best choice to promote Exalted...what if they get too busy fighting Thor?<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> ...And now I want an Artifact Crowbar with Evocations capable of empowering a posse...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T17:28:33-08:00","id":56457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt-M-McElroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/56144-if-onyx-path-had-a-volunteer-promotional-group-would-you-participate?p=56183#post56183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Wrecking Crew has run demos of Exalted, Cavaliers of Mars and other non-World of Darkness games. It often depends on which volunteer Storytellers are attending the event in question. Indeed, a good program would need lots of volunteers and OPP would need someone to coordinate with a large crew, vet the people and the process, follow-up with the team and conventions, deal with questions...all of which takes time and money (shipping isn't free, nor is printing). Where did you get that idea? The E3 Kickstarter got more advertising than several of the WoD KS projects. -MMM</div> </div> </div> </div> So, how does one join the Wrecking Crew? I can't find anything on thier site or Facebook on joining. <br /> <br /> I agree that it would take time and possibly some money to setup such a group. However, shoukd it work, it will produce more interest in the products, and thus return on the investment. <br /> <br /> Odd Canuck, I was hoping to guage and garner interest among the fans about setting up such a group. Rather than speaking to how things have gone in the past, let's brainstrom how we could create a group which helps promote these products we love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> This one is for all my Exigents...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/102-lordwyrmsbane","name":"LordWyrmsBane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T17:31:07-08:00","id":56458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/56144-if-onyx-path-had-a-volunteer-promotional-group-would-you-participate?p=56447#post56447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...And now I want an Artifact Crowbar with Evocations capable of empowering a posse...</div> </div> </div> </div>Bad Joke. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> But I do kinda like this idea as a seed. And given the fanbase I do think one of the better things that could happen is people applying some creativity to come up with scenarios that can be run in a convention/demo game timeslot. That's always been generally lacking in Exalted and is something that can help anyone wanting to run games.<br /> <br /> So what 4-8 hour adventure options can you come up with around that crowbar idea, given how Exalted games also have the habit of going off the rails shortly after they start?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T18:36:37-08:00","id":56504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/56144-if-onyx-path-had-a-volunteer-promotional-group-would-you-participate?p=56458#post56458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what 4-8 hour adventure options can you come up with around that crowbar idea, given how Exalted games also have the habit of going off the rails shortly after they start?</div> </div> </div> </div>During groundbreaking for a new building in Nexus, something.. strange was found. A vault, dated back to (Roughly) the Usurpation was found. The site was quickly cordoned off by the Guild, but one of the workers managed to grab something. A crowbar, forged from one of Isidoros' highest souls. The demon trapped within offered the worker, and some of his friends, power in exchange for certain considerations. And they accepted. Now with awoken Essence (and a small suite of basic, terrestrial-level charms) this &quot;Wrecking Crew&quot; is roaming the Streets of Nexus, causing general mayhem and havoc. Obviously, the PCs will want to stop this rampage, either to cease the destruction, or to grab the relic for themselves. <br /> <br /> Potential complications involve having to deal with (or <i>D</i><i>eal with) </i>other people who want to hunt down the &quot;Wrecking Crew&quot; themselves. Options include a Wyld Hunt who thinks they may be Anathema, a troupe of Fae who just think it would be fun to Hunt them Down, and a Yozi cult that wants to grab the Relic themselves (and negotiability, the Wrecking Crew with it). <br /> <br /> Just my thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T18:54:36-08:00","id":56510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/56144-if-onyx-path-had-a-volunteer-promotional-group-would-you-participate?p=56458#post56458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what 4-8 hour adventure options can you come up with around that crowbar idea, given how Exalted games also have the habit of going off the rails shortly after they start?</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://s30.postimg.org/kv5aeqx8x/Average_Exalted_Game.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Ain't that the truth. This particular instance pictured was taken from my last IRL chronicle; a political intrigue game that eventually became a chop-socky wuxia game.<br /> <br /> As for a plot hook, that reminds me of an early session I STed for, whereby through navigating the underground of Nexus, they found a giant shadowlands marking the grave of a Neverborn, and what to do to deal with it.<br /> <br /> Needless to say, things went up a creek REALLY fast, but still, a good starting off point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T19:04:46-08:00","id":56522,"title":"","content":"A few things:<br /> <br /> 1. I saw Exalted ads on multiple occasions, received numerous emails about the Kickstarter, and saw posts on various social media sites.<br /> <br /> 2. The more advertising the better, of course. Sucks to hear about the lack of response from some journalists.<br /> <br /> 3. I would LOVE to promote Onyx Path. Especially if their is some tier-like system involved that could some way show success.<br /> <br /> 4. I want an Onyx Path button.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 01-25-2014, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T00:40:14-08:00","id":56617,"title":"","content":"I'd be more than happy to be an Onyx Path volunteer, should such a thing ever materialise. I seem to be one of few convention GMs in the UK who runs World of Darkness games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T00:48:58-08:00","id":56619,"title":"","content":"That's not to say that WoD isn't popular at gaming clubs and groups over here. It's been remarked to me before and after games that it's a pity there's no official Onyx Path representation at the UK Games Expo, as Monte Cook is representing his line, Paizo and Chaosium may well be along this year and so on. We had C.A. Suleiman and Mark Rein Hagen at the expo last year (in unofficial capacities) but as there are UK-based Onyx Path freelancers I don't know if it would be worthwhile hiring one of them for the purpose. Dave Brookshaw and Stew Wilson spring to mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}